hat  we start with a lot of garlic  so the original midnight the midnight  pasta recipe starts with about nine to  eleven cloves of garlic but this is my  thought if you're eating pasta at 11  o'clock or 12 o'clock at night you don't  want a lot of garlic so this is how we  peel it really fast and remember I  always recommend using a very different  cutting board for your garlic than you  do for your everything else because the  the smell and the taste will stick in  your board so as you can see I minced  this garlic instead of actually slicing  it so we're going to add this garlic  right into the pot  now you're gonna want to cook it for  about two minutes you don't want it to  brown you just want it to cook so after  the garlic is cooked really nicely and  gets good and soft we're gonna add a  half a cup of chopped parsley which has  just an amazing smell we're going to add  about half of a teaspoon of red chili  pepper flakes of course more if you like  more less if you like less let me tell  you the key to all great sauces for  pasta it's adding some of the pasta  water back into the bowl so we have  reserved about a cup and a half of the  cooked pasta water the salty pasta water  and it goes right into this sauce we're  going to bring it up to a higher  temperature bring it up to a boil and so  now as it begins to heat up we are going  to add our pasta which we have drained  garlic smells so good  all the parsley is getting into the  pasta what we want to do is add another  half cup of the cheese just to thicken  it up and again cooking is intuitive and  instinctual so if you feel that it's  just a little too juicy which I just did  you're gonna add just a little bit more  cheese back into it and  we're just gonna sprinkle this with a  little bit of Parmesan cheese maybe put  a sprig of parsley right in the middle  and serve it right out of the same pot  that you cooked it in that's it  midnight pasta made with the fresh pasta  that we made just two weeks ago of  course it didn't hang out for two weeks  we cooked it right afterwards and we're  cooking and enjoying and hoping that you  are to enjoy your weekend everybody I  will have to try that thank you  Stephanie Buffy check out chef Andi  Bubbe on Facebook and Instagram and  thanks to Chapman automotive for  sponsoring that segment we'll be right  back
 

